  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: CareDisc 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'A cancer research team is exploring ideas for new treatments designed
    to reduce tumor growth. They meet with caregivers to learn what patients and
    their families go through day-to-day during treatment. When meeting with the
    research team, you explain how difficult it is for patients to manage treatments
    that require frequent hospital visits and/or long hospital stays.


    In this
    situation, what role does the caregiver play in the Discovery stage?'
  explanation: "At the discovery stage, caregivers can share insights that help scientists
    focus on developing treatments that better fit patients\u2019 real lives \u2014
    even before any drug is tested in humans. These insights can shape early research
    so future treatments are easier for patients and families to manage. By understanding
    these real-world needs early on, researchers can set goals that lead to more
    practical, compassionate innovations down the line."
  correctAnswer: 'B: Helping researchers understand real-life challenges patients
    face during treatment'
  incorrectAnswer1: 'A: Managing treatment dosage and side effects of the patient'
  incorrectAnswer2: 'C: Reviewing patient safety plans for upcoming clinical trials'
  incorrectAnswer3: 'D: Providing patient data to help hospitals decide which treatments
    to use'
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
